  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multiprofile + pca_n2000 + avgpool (config_002, acc 0.591) is the clear best so far, while image-only with resnet50 (config_010, acc 0.208) is very weak. No multimodal configuration has been tested yet. Question: Does combining the strong RNA signal with the weak resnet50 image signal via concatenation provide any complementary benefit over the best RNA-only baseline, or does the noisy image feature degrade performance? Why this is the best next experiment: It is the most direct multimodal extension of our best configuration (same RNA encoder, same profile/aggregation, same image encoder already characterized), giving a clean apples-to-apples comparison with config_002. The answer to this fundamental modality-combination question will determine whether all remaining budget should focus on RNA-only encoder improvements or whether the multimodal design space is worth exploring, making it the highest-information-gain experiment under a limited budget."
}

